values
  (212, 'How slice 3.4 is built (`slice-3-4.md`), from G13 and rules 12 and 13. Everyone who has written to the bot, owns an area or is waited on gets one direct message on weekdays, at the first reconcile after 9:00 in their Slack time zone and before noon, unless they said "stop briefs" (in a direct message, after a mention, or in the web app). The brief is built from the records with no model: what waits on them, what is theirs to decide, what happened in their areas, changes of their areas'' owners, and what they wait on, five lines a section with links; an empty brief is not sent. One row per person and local day is written before sending, so a brief goes once; a failed send is retried three times; ten briefs a reconcile run. `/brief` in the web app shows what a person''s brief would say now. Talking to the bot in a direct message is not in 3.4', 'Chosen in conversation as G13; the rest follows from rules 12 and 13. Building it without a model keeps it cheap and explainable, and a preview lets people see and correct what the bot would tell them before it does', 'active', 'the owner', '2026-11-26T00:00:00Z', 'import', '212')
on conflict (origin, origin_ref) where origin_ref is not null do nothing;
